Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone. In this section, I will guide you on the basic steps to find Delta using the GTest Automation tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.00,0:00:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I will open this tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,At the main interface, I will navigate to Analysis Support, and select Check Delta from Database, SharePoint.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.00,0:00:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, you will see the fields where I need to fill in the necessary information to operate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.00,0:00:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The first is the Analyze path.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I will provide the file path of the file that contains the modules I need to analyze.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,In this step, I will have two options.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.00,0:00:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The first option is to use File Analysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.00,0:00:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This File Analysis is the result of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.00,0:01:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the report file generated from the TPA Report Generation tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.00,0:01:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It contains a large number of modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.00,0:01:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The Testing Team uses this file for the analysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.00,0:01:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,For a smaller number of modules, I will choose Option 2.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.00,0:01:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I will use a template file to fill in the basic information of the module I need to analyze.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.00,0:01:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, I will input the path of that file into the tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.00,0:01:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, I will input the path of that file into the tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.00,0:01:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,(Inputting path)
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.00,0:01:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I will demo the first option.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.00,0:01:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will input the path of the analysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.00,0:01:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I have a File Analysis generated from the TPA Report Generation tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.00,0:01:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It contains many modules across various components, including both tested and untested modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.00,0:02:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The tool will process the modules whose MTVerdict value is "Undefined".
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.00,0:02:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The tool will support us to analyze those modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.00,0:02:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.00,0:02:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.00,0:02:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I copy the path of this file, then paste it into the first field (Analyze path).
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.00,0:02:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I copy the path of this file, then paste it into the first field (Analyze path).
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.00,0:02:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I copy the path of this file, then paste it into the first field (Analyze path).
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.50,0:02:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,(Processing)
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.00,0:02:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The second part is the database path.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.00,0:02:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the path of the folder that contains the database.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.00,0:02:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Whether loading using Snapshot or Stream using SharCC tool,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.00,0:02:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,we will look at our local directory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.00,0:02:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here is the database,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.00,0:02:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the folder is "DaihatsuCMP".
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.00,0:02:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will copy this path and input it into the tool here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.00,0:02:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I will create a folder.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.00,0:02:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I will create the "WorkSpace_1" folder.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.00,0:02:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This folder will contain the files
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.00,0:03:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and documents generated during the tool's process.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.00,0:03:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I have created the "WorkSpace_1" folder.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.00,0:03:14.00,Default,,0,0,0,,At the same time, I also put the File Analysis into this folder.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.00,0:03:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will copy the path of this folder.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.00,0:03:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Next is the Switch Setting part.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.00,0:03:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This refers to the CSV file generated
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.00,0:03:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,in the build config process using the tool SharCC.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.00,0:03:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will navigate to the database,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.00,0:03:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,go to Gen,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.00,0:03:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,select the corresponding config,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.00,0:03:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,then select Build,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.00,0:03:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and I will grab the path of this file,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.00,0:03:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,SwitchSettings CSV file.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.00,0:03:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I will input this path here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.00,0:04:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I will adjust the parallel threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.00,0:04:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I will have a maximum of 8 threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.00,0:04:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,By choosing the corresponding number,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.00,0:04:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We can help this tool process faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.00,0:04:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It corresponds to the Parallel Threads of this tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.00,0:04:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The Tool Development Team,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.00,0:04:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,they defined the maximum threads as 8,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.00,0:04:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,so I will choose the maximum value of 8 here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.00,0:04:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I will click Create Delta File.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.00,0:04:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.00,0:04:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.00,0:04:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the result after the first step.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.00,0:04:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here I have 3 types of modules:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.00,0:05:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will have Old, Old and no code, and New.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.00,0:05:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The result is also shown here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.00,0:05:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Relative to New, Old, and NoCode,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.00,0:05:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The number 28 corresponds to New,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.00,0:05:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,16 is Old, and 8 is NoCode.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.00,0:05:14.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I can observe the running process of the tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.00,0:05:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I can open the Terminal here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.00,0:05:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,To make it easier to observe, I can split the screen into 2 parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.00,0:05:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,To see the detailed results of the modules,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.00,0:05:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will go to the "WorkSpace_1" folder,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.00,0:05:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,then I will go to Output,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.00,0:05:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and select Open Module Info.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.00,0:05:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I will see all the modules listed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.00,0:05:57.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I have New modules,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.00,0:06:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Old modules,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.00,0:06:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and the rest are Old and no code.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.00,0:06:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The "New" type here refers to the modules
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.00,0:06:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,that do not have test scripts in the database
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.00,0:06:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,that we loaded from the Stream.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.00,0:06:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And the "Old" modules here are the ones that have test scripts
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.00,0:06:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and have been tested in the previous version.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.00,0:06:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Since they already exist
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.00,0:06:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,in the current database,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.00,0:06:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the tool will list them as "Old".
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.00,0:06:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And the "Old and no code" modules are the ones that have the TPA file,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and testing is done.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.00,0:06:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Those are Old and no code.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.00,0:06:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The tool helps me to list these modules as Old and no code.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.00,0:06:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, I close this file.
